$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: template-website/winning-trimming-com-au/seo-matrix-resolution
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-30"
summary: >-
  URL resolution engine for the SEO matrix. 9 URL levels across pillar, asset, product, region, and
  suburb dimensions. 7 resolvers: resolveMatrix (vessel-centric, depth 1-3), resolvePillarProduct
  (product across all vessels, depth 1-2), resolveRegionPage (pillar-scoped region),
  resolveRegionSuburbPage (pillar-scoped region+suburb), resolveAllPillarRegion (all-pillar region
  landing), resolveAllPillarSuburb (all-pillar suburb). Each validates pillar, checks segment
  existence against taxonomy collections with overrideAccess false, and enforces combination
  validity. Returns structured data or null (404). Also provides H1, description, and URL helpers
  for each level.
$system: template-website/system
$service: template-website/winning-trimming-com-au
intent: >-
  Turn SEO-friendly URLs into structured page data so the matrix templates can render consistent,
  optimised landing pages. Enforce that only valid pillar/asset/product/suburb combinations resolve
  — invalid ones 404, keeping the URL space clean for search engines.
status: built
implementation:
  primary: src/Matrix/matrix.ts
  test_code: ""
  test_code_status: none
see_also:
  - template-website/winning-trimming-com-au/seo-matrix-collections
  - template-website/winning-trimming-com-au/seo-matrix-templates
flows:
  - id: resolve-vessel-matrix
    name: Resolve vessel matrix URL
    description: >-
      URL like /marine/yachts or /marine/yachts/weather-covers or
      /marine/yachts/weather-covers/belmont
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: validate
        target: isValidPillar(pillar) and segments length 1-3
      - id: s2
        action: get
        target: asset-types where slug and pillar match, depth 2, limit 1
      - id: s3
        action: validate
        target: assetType found else return null
      - id: s4
        action: get
        target: if segment 2, service-types where slug and pillar match
      - id: s5
        action: validate
        target: productType must be in assetType.applicableProducts slugs
      - id: s6
        action: get
        target: if segment 3, suburbs where slug match (requires productType)
      - id: s7
        action: get
        target: siblingAssets same pillar, nearbySuburbs same region
      - id: s8
        action: return
        target: MatrixData with pillar, assetType, productType, suburb, region, depth, siblings, nearby
  - id: resolve-pillar-product
    name: Resolve pillar-level product URL
    description: URL like /marine/weather-covers or /marine/weather-covers/belmont (product across all vessels)
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: validate
        target: isValidPillar and segments 1-2
      - id: s2
        action: get
        target: service-types where slug and pillar match
      - id: s3
        action: get
        target: if segment 2, suburbs where slug match
      - id: s4
        action: get
        target: all asset-types for pillar, filter to applicableAssets containing product
      - id: s5
        action: validate
        target: applicableAssets length > 0 else return null
      - id: s6
        action: get
        target: nearbySuburbs same region if suburb present
      - id: s7
        action: return
        target: PillarProductData
  - id: resolve-region
    name: Resolve region landing URL
    description: URL like /marine/lake-macquarie (single segment after pillar)
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: validate
        target: isValidPillar and single segment
      - id: s2
        action: get
        target: regions where slug match
      - id: s3
        action: validate
        target: region.pillars empty or includes pillar
      - id: s4
        action: get
        target: parallel fetch suburbs, businesses, assetTypes for region+pillar
      - id: s5
        action: return
        target: RegionPageData
contracts:
  - id: pillar-validation
    description: Pillar slug must be in the 5 valid pillar values
    must_have:
      - >-
        isValidPillar checks against pillarValues (marine, automotive, caravan-and-rv,
        trade-and-industrial, commercial)
      - Invalid pillar returns null immediately
  - id: segment-count
    description: Segment count enforced per resolver
    must_have:
      - "resolveMatrix: 1-3 segments"
      - "resolvePillarProduct: 1-2 segments"
      - "resolveRegionPage: exactly 1 segment"
      - Out of range returns null
  - id: combination-validity
    description: Only valid combinations resolve; invalid ones 404
    must_have:
      - Product must be in asset applicableProducts (checked via slug list)
      - Suburb requires product (suburb without product returns null)
      - Region must be relevant to pillar (pillars empty or includes pillar)
      - PillarProduct with no applicableAssets returns null
  - id: override-access-false
    description: All taxonomy queries use overrideAccess false
    must_have:
      - >-
        asset-types, service-types, suburbs, regions, businesses queries all use overrideAccess
        false
      - Respects published/unpublished status and access rules
  - id: h1-generation
    description: Dynamic H1 derived from resolved data
    must_have:
      - >-
        matrixH1: depth 1 uses workSuffix from applicableProducts categories, depth 2 uses product
        title, depth 3 adds location
      - "pillarProductH1: pillarLabel + product, optionally + suburb/region"
      - "singularOf: uses singular field or strips trailing s (not ss)"
      - >-
        productCategory maps titles to Covers, Enclosures, Canvas, Sail Covers, Seats, Cushions,
        Interior, Upholstery
  - id: meta-description
    description: Meta description assembled from dimensions
    must_have:
      - "matrixDescription: vessel + product + suburb/region + brand tagline"
      - "pillarProductDescription: pillarLabel + product + suburb/region + brand tagline"
      - "Brand tagline: 'by Winning Trimming. Custom-made and repaired to last.'"
  - id: url-builder
    description: matrixUrl builds canonical URLs from segments
    must_have:
      - matrixUrl(pillar, assetSlug, productSlug?, suburbSlug?)
      - "Format: /pillar/asset[/product][/suburb]"
  - id: sitemap-excludes-suburb-urls
    description: >-
      sitemap.xml lists real pages, posts, projects, region landing pages and vessel/product pages
      only — never suburb-level matrix URLs.
    must_have:
      - No suburb-level URL appears in sitemap.xml
      - Region landing pages and vessel/product pages remain listed
  - id: suburb-pages-emit-noindex
    description: Resolved suburb-level pages emit robots index:false, follow:true; non-suburb levels do not.
    must_have:
      - >-
        matrix with suburb, pillar-product with suburb, region+suburb and all-pillar suburb all set
        noindex
      - Region and product pages stay indexable
tests:
  - id: valid-depth-1
    setup:
      pillar: marine
      segments: "[yachts]"
    expect:
      - depth: 1
        assetType: yachts
        productType: null
  - id: valid-depth-3
    setup:
      pillar: marine
      segments: "[yachts, weather-covers, belmont]"
    expect:
      - depth: 3
        suburb: belmont
        region: lake-macquarie
  - id: invalid-product
    setup:
      pillar: marine
      segments: "[yachts, nonexistent-product]"
    expect:
      - result: null
  - id: product-not-applicable
    setup:
      pillar: marine
      segments: "[yachts, earth-moving-seat-repair]"
    expect:
      - result: null
        reason: product not in asset applicableProducts
  - id: suburb-without-product
    setup:
      pillar: marine
      segments: "[yachts, belmont]"
    expect:
      - result: null
        reason: suburb requires product at depth 2
  - id: invalid-pillar
    setup:
      pillar: aerospace
      segments: "[yachts]"
    expect:
      - result: null
  - id: region-pillar-relevance
    setup:
      pillar: automotive
      region: "lake-macquarie (pillars: [marine])"
    expect:
      - result: null
        reason: region not relevant to pillar
decisions:
  - id: three-resolvers
    decision: Three separate resolvers (matrix, pillarProduct, region) rather than one mega-resolver
    rationale: >-
      Each handles a distinct URL shape and data structure. Keeps resolution logic readable and
      testable. Page component tries them in order.
    date: "2026-09-06"
  - id: null-on-invalid
    decision: Return null for invalid combinations (page calls notFound)
    rationale: >-
      Clean separation — resolver is pure data logic, page handles 404 response. Resolvers can be
      reused outside Next.js.
    date: "2026-09-06"
  - id: workcategory-h1
    decision: Group products into categories (Covers, Canvas, Seats etc.) for concise depth-1 H1s
    rationale: >-
      Listing 14 products in an H1 is unreadable. Grouping into max 3 categories keeps H1 concise
      and keyword-targeted.
    date: "2026-09-06"
  - id: depth-as-type
    decision: Model depth as a union type 1 | 2 | 3
    rationale: Compile-time safety — templates can narrow on depth knowing only 3 values are possible.
    date: "2026-09-06"
  - id: suburb-pages-noindex
    decision: Suburb-level matrix pages are noindex,follow and excluded from sitemap.xml.
    rationale: >-
      sitemap.xml previously advertised ~45,357 URLs, almost all suburb x service permutations.
      Measured 2026-09-30: 7.1 MB, 45,357 entries for a ~40-page site, each self-canonical, ~1.75s
      TTFB, cache-control: no-store. Search engines sampled a couple and stalled the crawl. Region
      landing pages (/{pillar}/{region}, /{region}) stay indexable and listed; suburb variants
      remain reachable but emit robots index:false, follow:true via buildMeta in
      [slug]/[...matrix]/page.tsx.
  - id: public-pages-isr-not-forced-dynamic
    decision: >-
      Public marketing routes (/, /our-work, /posts) render with ISR revalidate = 3600 instead of
      force-dynamic.
    rationale: >-
      Those routes were pinned dynamic = force-dynamic, so every crawler fetch was an origin render
      returning cache-control: private, no-cache, no-store. Verified live that ISR works on this app
      (/marine returns x-nextjs-cache: HIT with s-maxage=3600). Staleness is bounded to 1 hour,
      matching the existing revalidate = 3600 on [slug] routes.
